00:22:13.780 --> 00:22:25.320
<v Ira Glass>Emily Bonderer Cruz is an American. Her husband Raymundo-- she calls him Gordo-- is Mexican. When they met, he was here in the United States illegally. In fact, he had already been deported once and snuck back in.
<v Ira Glass>艾米丽·邦德勒·克鲁兹（Emily Bonderer Cruz）是美国人。她的丈夫雷蒙多（Raymundo）——她称他为Gordo——是墨西哥人。当他们相遇时，他非法留在美国。事实上，他已经被驱逐出境一次，又偷偷溜了回来。

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:46.370
<v Ira Glass>And the way that the law works, that means that the only way that he could live with her now right here in the United States with them married, is that he first needs to live outside the United States for 10 years. So after trying to live here in the States illegally for a little while, they decided they should move to Mexico. So they moved to Mexico.
<v Ira Glass>按照法律运作的方式，这意味着他现在只能和她一起住在这里，在美国，他们结婚了，他首先需要在美国境外住10年。所以在试图非法留在美国住了一段时间后，他们决定应该搬到墨西哥。所以他们搬到了墨西哥。

00:22:46.370 --> 00:23:00.640
<v Ira Glass>They chose Ciudad Juarez because it's a border town. Emily could earn a US wage just by commuting into El Paso every day right across the border. And that's what she does. While Ray works at a maquila, one of the factories-- there are tons of them-- on the Mexican side of the border.
<v Ira Glass>他们选择了华雷斯城，因为它是一个边境城镇。艾米丽只要每天通勤到边境对面的埃尔帕索，就能赚到美国的工资。这就是她所做的。而雷在马基拉（maquila）工作，就是边境墨西哥那一侧的工厂——那里有很多。

00:23:00.640 --> 00:23:29.850
<v Ira Glass>They moved to Juarez in 2010 at the height of the narco drug wars, when Juarez had the highest murder rate in the world, in the entire world. Emily started writing a blog about their life called The Real Housewife of Ciudad Juarez. And after reading it, radio producer Ann Heppermann gave her a recording kit and asked her just to keep a radio diary, documenting her everyday life to give the rest of us a sense of what it is like to be an American housewife right there.
<v Ira Glass>他们于2010年在毒品战争最激烈的时候搬到了华雷斯，那时华雷斯的谋杀率是世界最高的，在整个世界。艾米丽开始写博客记录他们的生活，名为《华雷斯城的真正主妇》。读过之后，广播制片人安·赫伯曼（Ann Heppermann）给了她一套录音设备，让她只写广播日记，记录她的日常生活，让我们其余的人了解在美国主妇在那里是什么感觉。

