<v Ira Glass>For me, it makes me happy that he can go and live a normal life that he couldn't live in the US. Or that I guess he could have, but it would've been so risky. You know, driving and paying for things that he couldn't do in the US. And even though he makes way less money here, he can be more of a man without having that income in other ways.
<v Ira Glass>对我来说，让我高兴的是他能去过一种在美国无法过的正常生活。或者我想他可以，但那会风险很大。你知道，开车和支付一些在美国不能做的事情。尽管他在这里赚的钱少得多，他可以作为一个男人，而没有其他方式的收入。

